# Bristlepack Sentry: "Defender" (CR 702.3b) and "as long as you control a creature with power 4 or greater, this creature can attack as though it
# didn't have defender". Bot1 controls only the Sentry (power 3) and a Llanowar Elves (1/1), so on T3 the Sentry cannot be declared as an
# attacker, though the Elves can be (the question is asked because one creature may attack) and deal 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Bristlepack Sentry
Llanowar Elves
Forest x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Bristlepack Sentry.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
! Bot1.Attack(Bristlepack Sentry > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield = Bristlepack Sentry; Llanowar Elves
